SoftGRE on Debian and Ubuntu
============================

The package provides dynamic IPv4 GRE Ethernet provisioning, VLAN-to-bridge
mapping, MAC permissions, a read-only TCP API and an optional status dashboard.
The daemon uses native Linux interfaces and requires root network privileges.

Configure /etc/softgred/softgred.conf for the capture interface, its local IPv4
address and VLAN-to-bridge mappings before starting the service. Kernel GRE,
VLAN and bridge support is required. The TCP API binds loopback by default.

    sudo systemctl enable --now softgred.service
    sudo systemctl restart softgred.service
    sudo systemctl status softgred.service

The daemon and dashboard are not enabled or started during package installation.
Python and logrotate are recommended dependencies. Enable the companion to start
the unprivileged dashboard with softgred and propagate daemon stops and restarts:

    sudo apt-get install python3 logrotate
    sudo systemctl enable --now softgred-web.service

The dashboard listens on port 8080. Its settings can be defined in
/etc/default/softgred-web using SOFTGRE_WEB_BIND, SOFTGRE_WEB_PORT,
SOFTGRE_API_HOST and SOFTGRE_API_PORT. Access the dashboard at
http://SERVER_IP:8080/index.html on a trusted management network.
Neither the dashboard nor the TCP API provides authentication.

Events append to /var/log/softgred.log and are mirrored to stderr/the journal.
Records identify remote IPs, tunnels, VLAN interfaces, bridges and learned MACs.
The package installs /etc/logrotate.d/softgred; SIGHUP reopens the log after
rotation. Adjust the rule if you change the log or PID path.

    sudo tail -f /var/log/softgred.log
    sudo journalctl -u softgred -u softgred-web -f

GRE learning does not provide subscriber authentication, automatic MAC roaming
or a DHCP server. Accepted frames use unkeyed GRE v0, Ethernet protocol 0x6558
and a single mapped inner VLAN. Use the guide for protocol and resource limits.

The README, complete English guide, logo and license are installed under
/usr/share/doc/softgred. The guide is docs/en_US/index.md relative to that
folder. The web assets and Python/PHP adapters are under
/usr/share/softgred/webinterface.

Build with dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b. The distribution-specific release
builder is scripts/build-deb.sh, run inside a matching disposable Linux image.
